MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SAE bolt assortment fits a concrete gap alongside my metric hardware and matches several thread sizes in my UNC rivet nut kit.",
    "Snap rings offer another way to secure mechanical parts alongside my cotter pins, while adhesive-lined heat shrink would help protect wire connections during repairs. Both have practical uses within the repair work I buy supplies for."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Loose bearing balls, landscape anchors, and a concrete grinding wheel require specific jobs I have no current need for; buying repair tools does not mean I need supplies for every kind of repair.",
    "Model glue and breadboards miss the purpose of my recent purchases: mounting, fastening, and mechanical assembly do not establish a need for model building or circuit prototyping."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in measuring and inspection tools seems to have been stretched into an interest in sound testing, without a task connecting them.",
    "My purchase of cutting wheels seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest concrete grinding, even though the material and job matter to whether I would use the accessory."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: SAE bolts matching my existing UNC rivet nuts are more useful than hardware that merely looks related.",
    "I already bought a substantial aluminum rivet assortment. More rivets are relevant, but I would check my stock before buying another kit; a complementary supply has a clearer immediate purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my mechanical repair needs but sometimes treated a broad connection to tools as enough, overlooking compatibility, existing supplies, and the specific job an item requires."
}
